# SmartDev Backend Configuration

## Environment Variables Template

Copy this to `.env.local` in the project root:

```env
# ==================== Server Configuration ====================
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=development
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ==================== Database ====================
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/smartdev
# For MongoDB Atlas:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/smartdev?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# ==================== AI Services ====================
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ==================== Authentication ====================
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_key_change_in_production_12345
JWT_EXPIRE=7d

# ==================== Email Configuration (Optional) ====================
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your_app_password
SMTP_FROM=noreply@smartdev.com

# ==================== Logging ====================
LOG_LEVEL=info
# info, warn, error, debug
```

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Local MongoDB Setup

**Option A: Using MongoDB Community Edition**

```bash
# macOS with Homebrew
brew tap mongodb/brew
brew install mongodb-community
brew services start mongodb-community

# Verify MongoDB is running
mongosh
```

**Option B: Using Docker**

```bash
docker run -d -p 27017:27017 --name mongodb mongo:latest
```

### 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
cd server
npm install
```

### 3. Setup Environment Variables

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
# Edit .env.local with your actual values
```

### 4. Start the Server

```bash
npm run dev  # Development with auto-reload
# or
npm start   # Production
```

### 5. Verify Server is Running

Visit `http://localhost:3001/api/health` in your browser. You should see:
```json
{
  "status": "OK",
  "timestamp": "2026-01-18T10:30:00.000Z",
  "uptime": 123.456
}
```

## Database Setup

### Create Collections Manually (Optional)

```javascript
// In mongosh console
use smartdev

db.users.insertOne({
  firstName: "Admin",
  lastName: "User",
  email: "admin@smartdev.com",
  password: "hashed_password",
  role: "admin"
})
```

### Using Mongoose Models

Models will automatically create collections when first document is inserted.

## Testing the API

### Using cURL

```bash
# Health check
curl http://localhost:3001/api/health

# Consultation endpoint
curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/consultation \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "message": "I want to build a web app for my business",
    "history": []
  }'

# Copilot endpoint
curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/copilot \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "message": "What services do you offer?",
    "history": []
  }'
```

### Using Postman

1. Create a new POST request to `http://localhost:3001/api/consultation`
2. Set header: `Content-Type: application/json`
3. Set body:
```json
{
  "message": "I want to build a web app",
  "history": []
}
```
4. Click Send

## Troubleshooting

### MongoDB Connection Error
- Ensure MongoDB is running: `brew services list`
- Check MONGODB_URI in .env.local
- For MongoDB Atlas, verify network whitelist includes your IP

### Gemini API Key Error
- Verify GEMINI_API_KEY is set correctly
- Get key from: https://ai.google.dev

### Port Already in Use
```bash
# Find process using port 3001
lsof -i :3001

# Kill the process
kill -9 <PID>

# Or use different port
PORT=3001 npm run dev
```

### CORS Error in Frontend
- Ensure CLIENT_URL matches your frontend URL
- Check that frontend is running on port 5173 (Vite default)

## Production Deployment

### Environment Variables for Production
- Set `NODE_ENV=production`
- Use strong JWT_SECRET (generate: `openssl rand -base64 32`)
- Use MongoDB Atlas for database
- Enable HTTPS for API calls
- Keep all sensitive keys in secure environment

### Build & Deploy
```bash
npm install --production
npm start
```

Use PM2 for process management:
```bash
npm install -g pm2
pm2 start index.js --name "smartdev-api"
pm2 logs smartdev-api
```
